      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "We report one case of symptomatic aneurysm of infrarenal abdominal aorta in a patient symptomatic for acute abdomen."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The patient was accepted at the Emergency Care Unit and the routine admission tests were taken. US of the abdomen revealed a <Situs Viscerum Inversus Totalis> (SVI) disposition of the organs and an aneurysm of the abdominal aorta below the renal arteries. Patient underwent an aorto-aortic straight graft"
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "In this case-report we show SVI cannot be considered a problem in the surgical treatment of symptomatic abdominal aortic aneurysms."
        }
      ]},
